    {
      "id": "be-s11-concentration-c1",
      "heading": "Two measures of concentration",
      "explanation_md": "**Four-firm concentration ratio (C4)**: the sum of the market shares of the **top four firms**.\n\n**C4 = w1 + w2 + w3 + w4**, where wi = Si / ST (firm sales over total industry sales).\n\n**Herfindahl-Hirschman Index (HHI)**: the sum of the **squared** market shares of **all** firms, **multiplied by 10,000**.\n\n**HHI = 10,000 x sum of wi²**",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [
        {
          "term": "Four-firm concentration ratio",
          "meaning": "Sum of the market shares of the top four firms in the industry",
          "source_ref": "be--session-11#6"
        },
        {
          "term": "Herfindahl-Hirschman Index",
          "meaning": "Sum of squared market shares of all firms, multiplied by 10,000",
          "source_ref": "be--session-11#6"
        }
      ],
      "exam_line": "C4 = w1 + w2 + w3 + w4; HHI = 10,000 x sum of wi².",
      "clarification": null,
