    {
      "id": "be-s11-concentration-c2",
      "heading": "Worked example: five banks",
      "explanation_md": "Five banks each have a **20 percent** market share.\n\n- **C4** = 0.2 + 0.2 + 0.2 + 0.2 = **0.8**\n- **HHI** = 10,000 x (0.2² + 0.2² + 0.2² + 0.2² + 0.2²) = 10,000 x 0.2 = **2,000**\n\nNote that C4 uses only four banks, while HHI uses all five.",
      "example_ids": [
        "be-ex-five-banks"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Five equal banks: C4 = 0.8, HHI = 2,000.",
