    {
      "id": "be-s11-concentration-c4",
      "heading": "Integration and the merger guidelines",
      "explanation_md": "| Type | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Vertical integration** | Various stages in producing a single product are carried out by one firm |\n| **Horizontal integration** | Merging the production of similar products into a single firm |\n| **Conglomerate merger** | Integrating different product lines into a single firm |\n\n**DOJ/FTC Horizontal Merger Guidelines** (based on HHI): a merger **may be challenged** if the **HHI exceeds 1800** (or would after the merger) **and** the merger **increases the HHI by more than 100**. The guidelines also recognize that mergers can bring **efficiencies** that lower prices.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Merger may be challenged if HHI exceeds 1800 and rises by more than 100.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
        {
          "id": "be-s11-concentration-q-e528f09e",
          "type": "mcq",
          "stem": "Merging the production of similar products into one firm is:",
