    {
      "id": "be-s11-concentration-q-d3ba9a06",
      "type": "long",
      "stem": "Define the four-firm concentration ratio and the HHI. Five banks compete in a local market, each with a 20 percent share. Calculate both measures.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "**C4** = sum of the market shares of the top four firms: C4 = w1 + w2 + w3 + w4, with wi = Si/ST.\n\n**HHI** = 10,000 x sum of the squared market shares of all firms.\n\nFive banks at 20 percent each:\n\n- C4 = 0.2 + 0.2 + 0.2 + 0.2 = **0.8**\n- HHI = 10,000 x (5 x 0.2²) = **2,000**\n\nAn HHI of 2,000 is above the 1800 level in the merger guidelines.",
